    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86148" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραιτώριον</span></b> , τό,
			= Lat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Praetorium, official residence of a governor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Matt.
				27.27
			</span></i>; later, of private <i>residences,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nov.</u>
				159
			</span></i>
			<u>Praef.</u>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>praetorian guard</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπαρχος
				πραιτωρίον, τοῦ π.,</span>
			=
			<i>praefectus praetorio</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				707
			</span></i> (Tyre, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.911
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>imperial household, Ep. Phil.</i><i><span class="en">
				1.13
			</span></i>.</div>
